framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0020:
  description "Dedicated reposition action, appropriate range bands, and engine-first spacing correction"

problem P1:
  |
    Production battles that spawn combatants in different battlefield areas
    lock pairRelations at separate_area and sight blocked. Counterpart
    strikes substitute to defend, lastActionResult describes the substitute,
    and speech freezes because the world never changes. There is no
    first-class spacing action. free_action positioning remains unfinished
    remaining work and spends an adjudication LLM.

premise DRIVER_DETERMINISM:
  |
    Spacing must be a server-owned world transition. It must not require a
    new provider route, retry, phrase ban, or free_action adjudication call.

premise DRIVER_BAND:
  |
    Legal striking distance is an appropriate band, not always-closer.
    Too close and too far are both illegal. A distant weapon opens; a
    melee weapon closes.

premise DRIVER_ENGINE_FIRST:
  |
    Prompt feedback is secondary. If a model still requests an illegal
    counterpart strike, the engine substitutes reposition toward that
    action's band instead of defend.

premise DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY:
  |
    Existing battles keep rest/defend/wait substitution. New rules bind
    only at battle creation. No backfill. Generic line_of_sight_blocked
    from cover or impaired vision is not treated as a spacing miss.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Considered options are: finish positioning only through free_action;
    add a dedicated deterministic reposition action; or keep substituting
    misses to defend and teach the model in prose. free_action still costs
    an adjudication LLM and does not yet update pair relations. Prose-only
    teaching leaves lastActionResult describing defend. Dedicated
    reposition is the narrowest engine path.

evidence E_PRODUCTION:
  |
    v0.22.0-rc.4 revision kshiai-api-00121-cik battle
    btl_03de9bec1693c9fffce4335cc5ba84b5 finished turn_limit 12, HP 109/109,
    maxHit 0%. Executed wait 36 and defend 36. Requested basic_attack/skill
    substituted for target_unlocalized or out_of_range. pairRelations stayed
    separate_area, sight blocked, updatedTurn 0.

evidence E_COUNTEREXAMPLE:
  |
    Stage battle btl_a90676928c9b47d618cc4812ccaf52ce spawned both actors
    in one area at near with clear sight. Strikes accepted and HP reached
    90/0. Spacing, not compact dialogue, is the failing layer for the
    zero-hit matches.

evidence E_WORLD:
  |
    docs/battle-world-model.md initializes different areas as separate_area
    with blocked sight. set_placement and set_pair_relation already exist.
    docs/battle-free-action-objectives.md lists pair/area updates as
    remaining work. ActionKind has no reposition member.

evidence E_AUDIT:
  |
    llmthink domain KshiaiRepositionAppropriateRangePlanAudit audited the
    implementation plan at fatal=0. It supported dedicated reposition and
    engine-first substitution, rejected prompt-only repair, global
    in-flight substitution, LOS-as-range, and auto-admitting the new kind
    through existing action norms.

decision D1 based_on P1, OPTIONS, DRIVER_DETERMINISM, E_WORLD, E_AUDIT:
  |
    Add ActionKind reposition. One accepted reposition performs at most one
    adjacent-area hop along frozen battlefield topology, or one in-area
    distance-rank change. It emits set_placement and/or set_pair_relation
    through applyBattleWorldTransition. free_action remains improvised
    object/posture work and is not the spacing primitive.

decision D2 based_on DRIVER_BAND, E_WORLD:
  |
    ActionFeasibilityConstraints keep reach as the maximum and gain optional
    minReach. separate_area and out_of_scene are never in-band for
    counterpart strikes. Bound snapshots without minReach keep max-only
    behavior.

decision D3 based_on DRIVER_ENGINE_FIRST, E_PRODUCTION, E_AUDIT:
  |
    On battles that bind pacingPolicy.spacingSchemaVersion 1, revalidateCharacterAction
    substitutes out_of_range and target_unlocalized counterpart intents to
    reposition toward the requested action's band. Do not map generic
    line_of_sight_blocked onto reposition. Feed observer-safe actionFeedback
    into the existing decideCharacterAction and advanceCharacterAgent
    decision frame. No new provider route.

decision D4 based_on DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY, E_AUDIT:
  |
    New pacing policies bind spacingSchemaVersion 1. Missing snapshot
    keeps rest/defend/wait substitution. lastAction naming, later-bucket
    fallback, and action-norm candidate mapping must include reposition.
    One public turn whose first beat is reserved wait can hop twice and
    share an area at far; a same_area hit may wait until a later beat.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-06 the product owner approved the audited plan
    "Reposition action, appropriate range, and failure-driven correction"
    through plan-mode acceptance, covering D1 through D4, engine-first
    substitution, optional minReach, battle-owned spacingRules, and the
    rejected alternatives in E_AUDIT.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    ADR-0020 is Accepted at this owner-approved revision. Acceptance
    authorizes local implementation and regression tests of D1 through D4.
    It does not authorize deployment, Stage observation, provider calls
    beyond existing battle routes, or compact-dialogue activation.
